 # Chorus aboveEditor widget can push chat transcript off-screen with no way to scroll back
 
-Found live during a Chorus room render test (tui-fullscreen-test), reported by Doug.
+Superseded by AGENT-256, filed independently and near-simultaneously by the coordinator with a more precise mechanism (CHORUS_TRANSCRIPT_ENTRY_LINE_LIMIT = 4, ~49-line worst case) and already prioritized HIGH with dev picking it up. Closing as WONTFIX-duplicate rather than leaving two open tickets for the same fix. See AGENT-256 for the actioned version; my candidate-fix list there is superseded by its more specific viewport-relative-budget direction.
 
-Symptom: as the Chorus room's sticky 'aboveEditor' widget (ChorusRoomTranscript, extensions/chorus/chorus-ui.ts) accumulates messages, it grows tall enough to push the actual agent chat transcript content off the top of the visible terminal area — and there is no way to scroll back to it. Terminal/TUI scrolling only applies to the main chat transcript pane, not the sticky widget region, and the sticky widget itself has no internal scroll or height clamp.
+---
 
-Root cause (grounded in code, not just observed): ChorusRoomTranscript.render() (chorus-ui.ts ~line 173) caps entries by COUNT via CHORUS_TRANSCRIPT_ENTRY_LIMIT = 12 (line 33), but does not cap by rendered LINE count. Each entry can wrap to multiple lines (formatChorusTranscriptEntryLines), so 12 entries -- or even fewer, if messages are long/multi-sentence -- can produce more terminal rows than the viewport has available. setWidget's 'aboveEditor' placement (per the tui skill's documented tradeoff: "sticky but full components") has no built-in max-height/scroll; it just claims whatever vertical space its render() reports, at the expense of the scrollable chat transcript area beneath/above it.
+# Activity Log
 
-Reproduction: open a Chorus room, have peers post a mix of long prose messages and short bursts (5-8+ messages, some multi-sentence) until the aboveEditor widget's total rendered line count exceeds a typical terminal height; observe the chat transcript scrolls off the top with no way to recover it via normal scroll.
+## 2026-08-07T19:29:03.339Z
 
-Candidate fixes (not evaluated/chosen -- Doug's call):
-1. Cap ChorusRoomTranscript.render() by an internal line budget (not just entry count), truncating/eliding oldest lines within the limit -- most direct fix, smallest surface.
-2. Give the aboveEditor widget its own bounded viewport height with internal scroll state, independent of the main transcript.
-3. Move the room transcript off 'aboveEditor' entirely onto the 'direct chat container injection' pattern the tui skill calls out as the preferred non-sticky, non-persistent option, keeping only the compact one-line status (ctx.ui.setStatus('chorus', ...), already confirmed working per Doug) as the persistent/sticky element.
-
-Not yet investigated: whether this is a Sandpiper-owned layout gap (chorus-ui.ts) or an upstream Pi TUI layout limitation (no max-height contract on setWidget). Needs a source check against Pi's TUI layout code before committing to a fix approach.
